      "changeReason": "New tool: left press mold for the inner tube sole (Shawn 2026-10-24: E6000 grabs too slowly and the cut tube lifts on the rounded edge; clamp the glued tube in a printed mold, leave it to cure, trim after). Cavity = the foot bottom offset 0.7 mm along the normal (tube 0.7 mm between ribs, 0.8 on a rib, measured by Shawn), one plane over the flat; it ends at the plane 2.3 mm, where the rim stays 0.7 mm from the foot so the rubber is not pinched and the excess leaves over the top. Dry, the foot lands on the flat floor and a pencil on the mold top marks the 3.0 mm glue line. Tabs 1.6 mm outside the foot, raised L. press-mold-check.json.",
